From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 22:30:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1605/3799] soh: rename func_80AACEE8 -> EnMk_FrogsIntro

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: the first line of the eye-drops sequence: it advances into the next line and starts the looping working animation.
Defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c
index b33bfaac2..f1513b0e9 100644
--- a/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c
+++ b/soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_En_Mk/z_en_mk.c
@@ -185,7 +185,8 @@ void func_80AACE2C(EnMk* this, PlayState* play) {
     this->flags |= 1;
 }
 
-void func_80AACEE8(EnMk* this, PlayState* play) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_80AACEE8: the first line of the eye-drops sequence: it advances into the next line and starts the looping working animation.
+void EnMk_FrogsIntro(EnMk* this, PlayState* play) {
     if ((Message_GetState(&play->msgCtx) == TEXT_STATE_EVENT) && Message_ShouldAdvance(play)) {
         Message_ContinueTextbox(play, 0x4000);
         Animation_Change(&this->skelAnime, &object_mk_Anim_000AC0, 1.0f, 0.0f,
@@ -259,7 +260,7 @@ void EnMk_Wait(EnMk* this, PlayState* play) {
                         break;
                     case EXCH_ITEM_FROG:
                         player->actor.textId = 0x4019;
-                        this->actionFunc = func_80AACEE8;
+                        this->actionFunc = EnMk_FrogsIntro;  // was func_80AACEE8 [LLM:HIGH]
                         Animation_Change(&this->skelAnime, &object_mk_Anim_000368, 1.0f, 0.0f,
                                          Animation_GetLastFrame(&object_mk_Anim_000368), ANIMMODE_ONCE, -4.0f);
                         this->flags &= ~2;
